            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "One minor thing around the meson option then looks fine."
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 420,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "We probably need to check the dbus_logging meson option here and only generate this if we're in dbus logger mode i suspect?"
                },
                {
                    "file": "meson.build",
                    "line": 420,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Patrick Williams",
                        "email": "patrick@stwcx.xyz",
                        "username": "williamspatrick"
                    },
                    "message": "There are still some dependency issue here that I'm going to fix shortly.\n\nDo we want to add a dbus_logging check here?  I have two reasons for not doing so:\n\n1. Generally things set up where all of the code compiles no matter what the settings are; dbus-logging is disabled by default which means we'll end up getting no coverage in CI if it gets broken.\n\n2. There was requested in the design that we add the OPENBMC_MESSAGE_ID in the journal when dbus-logging is disabled so that the old rsyslog path could be used.  This path (while not fully implemented right this moment) would also use the registries.\n\nhttps://github.com/openbmc/docs/blob/master/designs/event-logging.md#phosphor-logging"
                }
            ],
